    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1990-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For every \\(x\\in[2,3],\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} &|x-2|+|x-3|\\\\ &\\quad=(x-2)+(3-x)\\\\ &=1. \\end{aligned} \\] Thus the entire interval \\([2,3]\\) consists of solutions, so there are more than \\(3.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Interpret the two absolute values as distances on a number line",
        "Consider every \\(x\\) between \\(2\\) and \\(3\\)"
      ],
